=head1 DESCRIPTION

One authentication event that Amazon Cognito logged in a user pool with
threat protection active. Contains user and device metadata and a risk
assessment from your user pool.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 ChallengeResponses => ArrayRef[L<Paws::CognitoIdp::ChallengeResponseType>]

A list of the challenges that the user was requested to answer, for
example C<Password>, and the result, for example C<Success>.


=head2 CreationDate => Str

The date and time when the item was created. Amazon Cognito returns
this timestamp in UNIX epoch time format. Your SDK might render the
output in a human-readable format like ISO 8601 or a Java C<Date>
object.


=head2 EventContextData => L<Paws::CognitoIdp::EventContextDataType>

The user context data captured at the time of an event request. This
value provides additional information about the client from which event
the request is received.


=head2 EventFeedback => L<Paws::CognitoIdp::EventFeedbackType>

The C<UpdateAuthEventFeedback> or C<AdminUpdateAuthEventFeedback>
feedback that you or your user provided in response to the event. A
value of C<Valid> indicates that you disagreed with the level of risk
that your user pool assigned, and evaluated a session to be valid, or
likely safe. A value of C<Invalid> indicates that you agreed with the
user pool risk level and evaluated a session to be invalid, or likely
malicious.


=head2 EventId => Str

The event ID.


=head2 EventResponse => Str

The event response.


=head2 EventRisk => L<Paws::CognitoIdp::EventRiskType>

The threat evaluation from your user pool about an event. Contains
information about whether your user pool detected compromised
credentials, whether the event triggered an automated response, and the
level of risk.


=head2 EventType => Str

The type of authentication event.



